        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>Bisecting an angle requires: (1) Drawing an arc from the vertex to intersect both arms, (2) Drawing arcs from the intersection points to locate the bisector, and (3) Joining the vertex to the new intersection. <b>Measuring the angle with a protractor</b> is unnecessary and not part of the geometric construction.</p>",
